# Mobile — Expo + EAS

## Stack
- Expo SDK (latest stable that passes dependency vetting), TypeScript strict, **Expo Router**, React Query for
  server state, zustand (or similar) for local state, React Hook Form + zod, `expo-secure-store` for tokens.
- Backend: the project's server engine (Node.js/NestJS or Python/FastAPI) — the app never talks to the DB directly.
- Hebrew RTL: `I18nManager.forceRTL` decided at app start (with reload), `expo-localization`, logical styles
  (`marginStart`/`paddingEnd`), strings in i18n files.
- Install native-compatible packages with `npx expo install` (keeps versions aligned with the SDK); run
  `npx expo-doctor` in CI.

## Configuration
- `app.config.ts` reads `APP_VARIANT` (`development` | `preview` | `production`) to set name, bundle id/package,
  icon and API URL — so all three can be installed side by side.
- No secrets in the app bundle; only public config (`EXPO_PUBLIC_*`). Secrets stay on the server.

## EAS mapping to branches
| Branch | EAS build profile | Distribution | EAS Update channel |
|---|---|---|---|
| `develop` | `development` / `preview` | internal (dev client / internal testers) | `development` |
| `staging` | `preview` | internal — TestFlight + Play internal testing | `staging` |
| `main` | `production` | stores — `eas submit` to App Store Connect + Google Play | `production` |
- Builds are triggered from GitHub (EAS GitHub workflow / `expo/expo-github-action`), never from a laptop for staging/production.
- OTA updates (`eas update`) only for JS/asset changes compatible with the current `runtimeVersion`; native changes need a new build.
- Version: `version` (SemVer, user-facing) + auto-incremented build numbers (`autoIncrement` in eas.json, remote app version source).
- Store submission and phased release require human approval.

## Store compliance checklist (before first submission)
Privacy policy URL, Apple privacy "nutrition labels" and Google Data Safety form filled honestly, account
deletion in-app (required by both stores when sign-up exists), App Tracking Transparency prompt if tracking,
permissions with clear Hebrew purpose strings, screenshots per required device sizes, content rating, test
account for reviewers, Sign in with Apple if other social logins exist on iOS.

## Testing
Unit (Jest + React Native Testing Library), E2E with **Maestro** flows on preview builds (full suite level),
real-device checks on at least one iOS and one Android device before `main`. Crash reporting (Sentry) per variant.
